-01T22:16:18Z","closed_at":"2025-09-01T13:09:53Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.4.1.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3050 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6094) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-13400F (16 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nThis seems to be a line-breaking issue specific to Japanese punctuation when using Label nodes. In exported builds, the smart word wrapping occasionally places the Japanese full stop (。) at the start of a new line, which is typographically incorrect. This behavior does not occur in the editor preview.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. add ```Label``` to tree with any Japanese text as appropriate length (so that the character immediately before the full stop (。) appears exactly at the end of the line.).\n2. switch ```autowrap_mode``` as ```Word (Smart)```\n3. export game.\n4. execute exported game.\n5. the problem occurs.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[reproduction.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22057608/reproduction.zip)\n","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_